{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789817611,"nonce":"yGjqX6axuFV8MQITJVbxt42jPRw=","title":"a same-package type referenced before its module lowers decays to this.Type","message":"`haxe/Int64.hx` calls `Int64Helper.parseString(sParam)` with no import (same package). `haxe.Int64` and `haxe.Int64Helper` import each other, so one lowers first; when it is Int64, `Int64Helper` resolves to nothing and the abstract-body fallback turns the bare name into `this.Int64Helper` -- a Dynamic field read on the i64. The call becomes a by-name dynamic dispatch that lowers to nothing; `haxe.Int64.parseString` compiles to `ret void` (W0020 \"Return with no value\") and `Int64.parseString(\"42\")` traps.\n\nFix: an unresolved capitalised bare name whose `\u003ccurrent package\u003e.\u003cname\u003e` the namespace resolver can read as a declaration gets the placeholder an `import` would mint (`create_import_placeholder`, added to the root scope), so `Type.method(..)` is a static call linked by qualified name.\n\nAlso in this change: the multi-segment static call path (`haxe.Int64.fromFloat(..)`) accepted only `SymbolKind::Class`; an abstract went to the instance path as a method call on the type. And `import haxe.Int64.*` wildcard statics: the bare call is rewritten as `\u003cowner\u003e.name(..)` on the owner's bare name when that resolves to the owner, else its qualified path.\n\nFollow-ups seen in TestInt64 once it compiles (12 FAILCHECK, was COMPILE_FAIL): `0xFFFFFFFF` literal reads as 4294967295 not -1; `exc` checks see no exception from parseString on bad input.","files":null}]}